## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design a scalable, multi-tenant data ingestion architecture across AWS accounts while addressing security, reliability, and cost optimization challenges.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles with trust relationships
- Tenant isolation through data partitioning and access controls
- Exactly-once processing using idempotent operations
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Firehose, and S3 integration
- KMS encryption and data retention policies
- Cost management through throttling and lifecycle strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Idempotent processor using DynamoDB for deduplication
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const dynamodb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const failures = [];

  for (const record of event.Records) {
    const { tenantId, sequenceId, data } = JSON.parse(record.kinesis.data);
    const tableName = process.env.DDB_TABLE;

    try {
      // Check if sequence already processed
      const result = await dynamodb.get({
        TableName: tableName,
        Key: { tenantId, sequenceId }
      }).promise();

      if (result.Item) {
        continue; // Skip duplicate
      }

      // Process data...
      await processData(tenantId, data);

      // Mark as processed
      await dynamodb.put({
        TableName: tableName,
        Item: { tenantId, sequenceId, processedAt: Date.now() }
      }).promise();

    } catch (error) {
      failures.push({ itemIdentifier: record.kinesis.sequenceNumber });
    }
  }

  return { batchItemFailures: failures };
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests proficiency designing fine-grained, scalable access controls for multi-tenant data lakes using ABAC, tags, and policy syntax.

## Key Concepts
- IAM tags and aws:PrincipalTag
- Resource policies with aws:RequestTag and stringEquals conditions
- S3 bucket prefixes per tenant and least privilege
- Testing cross-tenant access and tag revocation

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy (IAM role)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantAccess"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Permission policy
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Bucket policy (alternative strict guard)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantAccess"},
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"s3:ExistingObjectTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

